deploy_gate:
  instruction: Before deploying TinyRustLM.MiRust.com or TinyRustLM.com, update this developer portal, MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, and any remaining SLMComposer.com redirect/public export surfaces to match the deployed source behavior.
  requirements:
    - Keep source options, .slm verification claims, model documentation, and no-server-model-byte boundaries current.
    - Document Hugging Face metadata/conversion handoffs, shared simple/advanced source-row actions, MiniModel `prepare-peer-share` sender packages, MiniModel `add-peer-source` late peer-source publication, MiniModel `write-peer-source-announcement` portable availability metadata, same-origin checksum-bound catalog announcement feed routes, MiniModel `apply-peer-source-announcements` maintainer drift checks, MiniModel `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` batch metadata publication, MiniModel `write-catalog-snapshot` metadata reuse, local `models.v0.json` loading, catalog-listed MiniModel peer sources, self-locating `.minimodel-peer-import.ps1` receiver scripts, and known-peer MiniModel serve/fetch handoffs when TinyRustLM app behavior changes; do not imply broad P2P discovery, relays, or project-hosted model bytes until implemented.
    - Keep TinyRustLM.com documented as the root app route; do not describe /app/ as the canonical TinyRustLM.com path.
    - Keep the former standalone runtime documentation lane documented only as retired/preserved content under /docs/runtime-portal/.
    - Keep SLMComposer.com documented only as a retired or redirecting app identity, not the canonical public app.
    - Run relevant pointer audits and git diff --check before packaging or deployment.
required_private_read_order:
  - workspace.uai
  - .uai/index.uai
  - .uai/totem.uai
  - .uai/taboo.uai
  - .uai/talisman.uai
  - .uai/file-handoff.uai
  - .uai/intake-outcome-ledger.uai
  - .uai/short-term-memory.uai
current_state:
  - TinyRustLM.MiRust.com is the TinyRustLM developer portal.
  - TinyRustLM.com is the root-domain browser-local Rust/WASM app route.
  - Hugging Face search rows in TinyRustLM are metadata until MiniModel metadata names an admitted .slm with peer-offer proof and a catalog-listed or user-supplied consenting peer source, or the user locally converts source bytes with Rust, verifies the .slm, and imports it through the browser file picker.
  - When Hugging Face metadata includes safe `.safetensors` sibling names, TinyRustLM may show those source-file hints in rows and local conversion scripts, but it must not download, proxy, or treat them as runnable model bytes.
  - TinyRustLM's simple and advanced Hugging Face rows share action/source-note helpers so `P2P Import`, `Set Peer URL`, `Start Conversion`, disabled-P2P fallback, and source-file hints stay aligned.
  - TinyRustLM's simple Hugging Face lane defaults P2P on, shows P2P Import only for MiniModel matches with peer-offer proof plus validated catalog peer source or saved Known peer URL, shows Set Peer URL for proof-ready rows without a known source, shows Start Conversion otherwise, and shows one list-level warning when P2P is disabled.
  - Start Conversion generates a self-contained local Rust handoff: save request JSON for audit/reuse, embed that JSON in the script so it can recreate the sidecar if missing, resolve workspaces/source files from environment variables, nearby paths, or a reviewed `.safetensors` beside the script; convert/pack source bytes into `.slm`; validate it; call MiniModel `prepare-peer-share`, discover the generated manifest, catalog entry, and peer-piece directory, then optionally use MiniModel `add-peer-source` for a direct with-peer entry; optionally write `write-peer-source-announcement` metadata for a catalog maintainer; rely on `apply-peer-source-announcements` for maintainer drift-checked merges or `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` for batch publication; then call MiniModel `write-catalog-snapshot` when publishing already-merged entries to create loadable metadata-only `models.v0.json` for reuse.
  - TinyRustLM exposes the generated snapshot route as `Local models.v0.json` / `Load Local Catalog`; once loaded, Hugging Face search uses that local metadata before the default MiniModel catalog, and matching rows with peer sources become `P2P Import`.
  - TinyRustLM may follow same-origin, SHA-256-bound peer-source announcement feed routes declared by a loaded catalog; those feeds are metadata only, fail closed on peer availability if verification fails, and never fetch project-hosted model bytes.
  - Proof-ready MiniModel rows use metadata-only catalog entries with peer_hint_status=peer-offer-ready-known-peer-needed, peer_import_status=request-script-ready, and optional peer_source_count/peer_sources metadata; P2P import rejects project/Hugging Face hosts and uses self-locating local Rust `import-peer-request` receiver execution for fetch, assembly, verification, and import receipt before browser import.
  - TinyRustLM can prepare local MiniModel share metadata after verified .slm import; MiniModel can export/serve/fetch/reassemble known-peer pieces, while broader peer discovery/relay remains later.
  - The former standalone runtime documentation corpus was preserved under docs/runtime-portal/ with a checksum manifest while its separate documentation authority is retired.
  - SLMComposer.com is no longer the canonical public app identity.
  - The live public-safe export is verified.
  - Direct public .uai and agent-file-handoff access is denied.
